      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/03-bony-tongues/gnathonemus-petersii-peters-elephantnose-fish/",
      "html": "<p>Most often this bizarre mormyrid is kept as a single specimen. This is because small groups of this fish most often do not do well in the long term, and they can mob each other, even to death. In the wild, however, these animals, up to 30 cm long but rarely longer than 15 cm, sometimes form really large schools. In the source's facility they are kept in groups of about 50 animals in tanks of 200 x 60 x 60 cm. Here the elephantnose fish forms schools and shows a schooling behaviour that is hardly seen in any other aquarium fish.</p>"
    }
